  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 sets a 7% permanent limit reached only after a seven-year transition with no interim numeric cap, which is the main weakening and largely protects Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 keeps the mandatory 8-per-100k recall trigger with no transition, which still applies to Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9). Per-model results go directly to purchasers but are not published to the public, and S3 and S4 sit inside the acceptable ranges."
